-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Auf Wiedersehen Monty
  Publisher   Gremlin Graphics, 1987
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Auf Wiedersehen Monty (1987)(Gremlin Graphics
              Software)[128K].z80
  MD5         fe2564a9bf18456d0857806c6219125f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing
              1.2: Keeps the CPU speed you chose (F8): the sprite updates used
              to drop the Next back to 3.5 MHz
              1.3: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off again:
              1.2 was built without it

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 to 4 choose the controls, 0 starts.
              Monty and the creatures in each room are hardware sprites over
              the pixels the game still draws: the creatures in their own
              colours, Monty in white, so nobody takes on the colour of the
              scenery they pass and the coloured squares the game painted
              behind every figure are gone. Known difference: the game kept a
              figure's pixels off where they touch scenery ink, for
              legibility; the sprites show each figure whole. The added work
              runs at 28 MHz; at most about 2% more per update at the original
              speed.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Aliens do not kill
   3  No crushers
   4  Water does not kill
   5  No tickets needed to fly

  From an archive .pok, each checked against this release's code: the lives
  store made a NOP, the alien collision test's first byte made RET, the
  crusher routine's first byte made RET, the water death's LD A,7 made LD A,0,
  and the ticket test's RET Z made a NOP (the .pok marks that one for the 48K
  version; the same code sits at the same address in this 128K release).

