-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification against a 321,815-frame
              recording (a whole playthrough); Tang FPGA board: loads with
              DivMMC automap on and sprites left by another program, and plays
              from the menu into the first room. Played by the owner on a ZX
              Spectrum Next (KS3), 2026-11-26: good.

  Replay      IDENTICAL on a 321,815-frame recording through 571 room draws:
              at every hook original and patched code compared from the same
              state (every register but R, all RAM), every sprite against its
              figure record after each of 155,935 figure loops, and every
              pixel the game's own drawer put into a figure's cells inside
              that figure's sprite (61.1 million pixels); 63 unit cases; 7
              deliberately broken builds rejected

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: played by
              the owner, good

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
